    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cefa1f34_3fe4499f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T11:00:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This approach seems odd to me, it\u0027s not really necessary to create a tag with that name since git can resolve `v3.2.14-43-g13eabbd5f1` without an explicit tag with that name on commit `13eabbd5f1`.\n\nNevertheless I think this fix is correct, `ReceiveCommand#getRefName` returns the name of a git ref, not an arbitrary commit-ish, hence calling `#findRef` instead of `#resolve` is the right thing to do here and should be also faster. If Gerrit wants to prohibit pushing a tag with a name created by git describe it should do so explicitly and not as side effect of using `#resolve`.",
      "parentUuid": "c65e05ce_a7268e1a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 35
      },
